error[LIMIT006]: this compiler cannot lower `<c:mark>` from namespace `urn:example:custom` inside `<state>`
 --> tests/ui/multi-diagnostic-ordering.scx:6:6
  |
4 |   <state id="ready">
  |    ----- this compiler lowers only SCXML children of `<state>`
5 |     <transition event="finish, abort" target="don"/>
6 |     <c:mark value="not-an-integer"/>
  |      ^^^^^^ element from another namespace
  |
  = note: this is a limit of this toolchain, not an SCXML rule: SCXML 1.0 allows elements from other namespaces in its content models (the W3C schema's `##other` wildcards), but the compiler lowers them only as executable content (custom actions in `<onentry>`, `<onexit>`, `<transition>`, `<finalize>`, `<if>`, or `<foreach>`) and rejects them anywhere else rather than drop them silently
  = help: to compile the document with this toolchain, move the element into executable content, or remove it
help: remove `<c:mark>`
  |
6 -     <c:mark value="not-an-integer"/>

